# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00203 M5: rebuilds ccy-teams only (no launcher or image change, so no ccy version bump
# and no image rebuild). In `ccy-teams`, Tab now shows the running sessions: add one to a team
# (Ctrl-A), remove it (Ctrl-X), change its role (Ctrl-O), move it, attach it, or repair a
# stopped seat keeper, each by running the `ccy-teams session` command for you. Running sessions
# are not touched. Plan 00201 Task 2.15 rides on the same play: Enter on a team, then Edit
# settings, opens one screen of the team's fields to change, save and apply (ACCEPTANCE-owner.md
# step 13). It does bump the launcher and image (CCY 3.99.10.2, container 2.75.2), because
# declare.py is in the image's agent_bus copy: the next ccy launch rebuilds the image once.
# Running sessions are not touched.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00201 Task 2.15: helpers/agent_bus/declare.py gained `settings` and `set`, and it is part
# of the admin zipapp, so every team reads "out of date (software)" until this runs. It installs
# the new zipapp and stamps each team again. No unit, firewall or rendered config changes, so no
# homeserver is restarted.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00203 acceptance again, on the M5 ccy-teams: every milestone in turn (M2, M1, M3, M4,
# then R1-R9; throwaway teams acc-m3a, acc-m3b, acc-m4a, acc-m4b, acc-robust and throwaway
# headless sessions in ccy's tmux, all removed after). M4 (e) re-proves `ccy-teams session
# list`, whose code the picker's view now shares; the picker itself is the owner's steps,
# ACCEPTANCE.md M5 (a) to (f), on a terminal. A bus process is now its program (python3
# running the pingbus or agent-bus entry point), so claude, whose argv names the plugin
# directory .../plugin/pingbus, no longer counts as one in M2 (c), M2 (e) or M1 (b). Each run
# removes its sessions' keeper reports (.claude/ccy/pingbus/sessions/<name>/), and first the
# ones earlier acceptance runs left (m1-plain-, m2-plain-, m2-nobus-, m3-hot-, m4-a-, m4-b-
# names only, never a running session's): the two m2-plain-* reports on this host go. Needs
# ccy launched interactively here once (Quick Launch).
00203-teams-hot-control-and-robustness
# Plan 00161 acceptance again (U20's seated headless sessions, then M2.11's named session).
# Its teardown now removes the keeper reports of every seated session it launched: the M2.11
# named session's (with its registry record) and, the review's B1, the unnamed M2.0 sessions'
# reports, which are named after their containers (each one whose name was not there before
# M2.0). The prerequisites remove u20-named-* reports an earlier run left (none of a running
# session) before M2.0 records the checkout, so M2.10 compares it strictly and passes on a
# clean run, whatever container numbers the sessions get.
00161-agent-team-bus-matrix/acceptance.bash
